    "body": "@TimothyGu What kind of specification bug are you talking about? But as I understand you, you are talking about the fact that the **custom element** is an **HTML element**. Right?\r\n\r\nNamespace (\"`http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml`\") refers to different parts of the document, but since we're talking about HTML, we need an HTML document - https://www.w3.org/TR/html5/ and there's no definition for **custom elements**. Then how does the namespace (\"`http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml`\") refer to **custom elements** if it is not in the w3 specification?",
