    "body": "@dSalieri \r\n\r\n> you are talking about the fact that the custom element is an HTML element. Right?\r\n\r\nYes that's right.\r\n\r\n> Namespace (\"`http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml`\") refers to different parts of the document, but since we're talking about HTML, we need an HTML document - https://www.w3.org/TR/html5/ and there's no definition for **custom elements**. Then how does the namespace (\"`http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml`\") refer to **custom elements** if it is not in the w3 specification?\r\n\r\nHmm, I'm not quite sure what you are referring to here. Namespaces are there only for legacy purposes. The fact that the namespace for HTML elements (including custom elements) is under `w3.org` and `xhtml` doesn't quite matter. And with regards to HTML, WHATWG's spec _is_ HTML.",
