    "body": "@TimothyGu It seems to me that I do not quite understand what \"namespace\" means in HTML or XML. And in view of this, I incorrectly interpret what is written in the specification. How does the program understand one or the other namespace? Under each namespace there must be some rules for the program to know which set of rules or instructions to apply. Or not? If not so, then explain please.\r\n\r\nAs far as I know, namespace in XML is used to not confuse specific data that will be used through CSS or DOM.\r\n\r\nCan you explain what you mean by this sentence: \"Namespaces are there only for legacy purposes\"?\r\n\r\nAs for the specification - yes, I understand that the current specification is whatwg. But when you read whatwg or w3c, then these specifications refer to each other (as in this case when it comes to namespace - http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml)\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
