    "body": "@tabatkins Hmm, I think I started to understand something. That is, any HTML elements written in the HTML document are in the namespace http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml, and the SVG elements are in the namespace https://www.w3.org/2000/svg. And how does the browser understand what namespace it works with if there are 2 of them at once: html and svg?  Are the instructions for these namespaces in the browser? And please clarify the situation with (`<html:script>` and `<svg:script>`) - is it somehow possible to use it in your html code? I did not find such syntax in html.",
